#. module: woow_paas_platform
#: model:ir.model.fields,help:woow_paas_platform.field_sh_subscription_subscription__woow_last_low_balance_mail_id
msgid ""
"The queued low-balance notification for this cycle. The date marker alone "
"cannot tell \"queued\" from \"delivered\": force_send=False only enqueues, "
"and a mail that fails delivery parks at state=exception which Odoo's "
"scheduler never retries (process_email_queue only picks up outgoing). "
"Keeping the carrier lets the next cron tick re-send instead of going silent "
"for the whole renewal cycle (#389). state=cancel is an explicit \"do not "
"send\", not a transient failure, so it is not retried. Retries are bounded "
"by _LOW_BALANCE_RETRY_WINDOW_DAYS rather than by the dunning threshold "
"(which may legitimately be 0). The mail is created with auto_delete=False so "
"the carrier survives — Odoo unlinks auto_delete mails not only on success "
"but also on mail_email_invalid / mail_email_missing. Empty means legacy data "
"(pre-.89) or a manually purged mail; both are conservatively treated as "
"delivered so upgrading does not re-notify every overdue tenant at once."
msgstr ""

